<section class="quotes" id="quotes">
  <div class="quotes__slideshow" id="quotesSlideshow">
    <div class="quotes__slide is-active">
      <p class="quotes__text">"Everything worth having in life takes longer than you want, hurts more than you expected, and demands more out of you than you were prepared to give."</p>
      <p class="quotes__chapter">Chapter: Why Grit Matters</p>
    </div>
    <div class="quotes__slide">
      <p class="quotes__text">"People have forgotten how to stay with something long enough to become exceptional at it. They chase novelty instead of mastery. They confuse fleeting motivation with real commitment."</p>
      <p class="quotes__chapter">Chapter: Introduction</p>
    </div>
    <div class="quotes__slide">
      <p class="quotes__text">"The strongest people alive aren't the ones who never quit anything, they're the ones who know exactly when quitting is wisdom and when it's just weakness wearing a disguise."</p>
      <p class="quotes__chapter">Chapter: The Moment to Quit</p>
    </div>
    <div class="quotes__slide">
      <p class="quotes__text">"Being able to tolerate boredom is key to having grit because every worthwhile pursuit comes with tedious work. Meaningful results are usually built through thousands of repetitions long before any outcome happens."</p>
      <p class="quotes__chapter">Chapter: Boredom Tolerance</p>
    </div>
    <div class="quotes__slide">
      <p class="quotes__text">"The second something you're chasing requires sustained discomfort — and anything worth having always does — your mind works against you."</p>
      <p class="quotes__chapter">Chapter: The Mechanisms of Quitting</p>
    </div>
  </div>

